<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29101" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mīmus</span></b> , i, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῖμος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A mimic actor, mime</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. de
				Or. 2, 59, 242</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oratori minime convenit distortus vultus
					gestusque: quae in mimis rideri solent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 6, 3, 29</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. A. A. 1, 501</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nobilis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					8, 198</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A mimic play, mime, farce</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mimi exitus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Cael. 27, 65</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tutor, mimus vetus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					de Or. 2, 64, 259</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mimos scribere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 2, 497</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mimorum scriptor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 10, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mimos commentari,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 11, 6, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mimum agere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 39</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Juv. 13, 110</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mimus quis melior plorante gula?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 5,
					157</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>any thing farcical,
				pretended, unreal</i>.—Of the sham triumph of
			Caligula, <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 45</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">commendationis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 12, 10, § 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">humanae vitae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 80, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mimus et simulatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 26, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
